From owner-pc532%daver@mips.com Wed Mar 28 18:50:45 1990
Reply-To: pc532@daver.bungi.com
Date: Wed, 28 Mar 90 10:46:44 pst
From: Bruce Culbertson <culberts@hplwbc.hpl.hp.com>
To: pc532@hplwbc.hpl.hp.com
Subject: New EPROM

Hello pc532'ers,

Here is a new EPROM image.  The major change is in the code for
running and single stepping "code under test".  It is supposed to
work now.  I have tested it, but remember, I do not have a quality
assurance department at my disposal.  So be skeptical and let me
know when you find things which are broken.  There are many minor
changes, like slightly improved help messages.

I confess I have not run this exact set of bits.  Instead, I link
it to run in RAM and download it using an older version in my EPROM.
This requires very minor changes like skipping the code which
initializes the memory parity.  I very much doubt this image has
serious problems.  However, if it is a nuisance for you to get an
EPROM burned, you might want to wait until someone gives it the
thumbs-up.

There is another reason you might want to wait.  In the next week or
so I hope to add SCSI commands.  I already have the commands working
on my 32016 and am waiting for Dave Rand's pc532 "DMA" code.

I am sending this version out now because I know there are many
people who can easily program their EPROM's and are quite anxious to
have "run" and "step" working.

Here's some weird behavior I found.  The EPROM's sent out with the
kits only initialized 4 megabytes of DRAM.  It took an almost
imperceptible amount of time to do it.  Dave and George estimated
that initializing the whole 32 megabyte DRAM space would take
about a second.  I tried this and it took twenty seconds.  Any
ideas why?  This image initializes 8 megabytes and I have not
timed it.

I will post a few of the monitor source files for those who want
to know how to boot the machine and talk to the uart's.  Unless
there are objections, I will not post all the sources until the
SCSI commands are in them.

Bruce Culbertson
---------------------------------------------------------------
